\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Figure recreated from \citet  {hofton1996post}, their Figure 16: rift-perpendicular horizontal displacements at Krafla, 1987--1992, with $1\sigma $ error bars (black circles), and the \citet  {foulger1992post} diffusion model $u(x,\tau ) = b\,\mathrm  {erfc}[x/(2\sqrt  {\kappa \tau })]$, differenced between $\tau _i=12$ and $\tau _f=17$~yr after the onset of the 1975--1984 rifting sequence, at the $\kappa =3.11$~m$^2$~s$^{-1}$, $b=1.27$~m best-fit parameters reported by \citeauthor  {hofton1996post} (red curve; a constant reference-frame offset, not a free shape parameter of the model, is added to match the digitized profile). The systematic misfit at near- and far-field stations simultaneously ($\chi ^2_r \approx 10$) leads \citet  {hofton1996post} to argue that a viscoelastic half-space, rather than simple diffusion, is needed to explain the post-rifting deformation field.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
