\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Model geometry. The brittle elastic plate (thickness $H$, Young's modulus $E$, Poisson's ratio $\nu $) overlies a Newtonian viscous half-space (viscosity $\eta $). Dike intrusions open the rift by $b$ at intervals $T$ (Appendix~\ref {app:b2}); the surface displacement $u(x,t)$ is positive away from the rift axis. The parameter $a = EH/[2\eta (1-\nu ^2)]$ sets the characteristic velocity that couples elastic and viscous deformation.}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:schematic}{{2}{3}{Model geometry. The brittle elastic plate (thickness $H$, Young's modulus $E$, Poisson's ratio $\nu $) overlies a Newtonian viscous half-space (viscosity $\eta $). Dike intrusions open the rift by $b$ at intervals $T$ (Appendix~\ref {app:b2}); the surface displacement $u(x,t)$ is positive away from the rift axis. The parameter $a = EH/[2\eta (1-\nu ^2)]$ sets the characteristic velocity that couples elastic and viscous deformation}{figure.2}{}}
