\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Surface velocity profile (top row of each block) and interior velocity field (bottom row; arrows coloured by speed magnitude, via Equation~\ref {eq:halfspace_kernel}) for the Maxwell STEP response (top two rows) and the Maxwell CSS (bottom two rows), at six illustrative recurrence times $\tau $. Both rows are normalised by $\tau _R/b$ (the Maxwell relaxation time), on the same colour scale so arrow colour is directly comparable between STEP and CSS; arrow length is scaled independently within each block for visual clarity. The dashed vertical line in each surface-profile panel marks the fixed Maxwell length $\ell _M = a\tau _R$ (Equation~\ref {eq:maxwell_length}), rather than the viscous $L=a\tau $, since $\ell _M$ does not depend on $\tau $. The single grid point directly above the dike is omitted from the quiver because the near-source field there is disproportionately large relative to the rest of the domain.}}{11}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
